## Executive Summary

Kimi K3 is Moonshot AI's flagship mixture-of-experts model from their Kimi series, launched July 16, 2026, designed for complex, long-horizon agentic workflows. It features a massive 2.8 trillion total parameters (104 billion active per token), 1M token context window, native visual understanding, and exceptional performance on coding and agentic benchmarks (88.3% on Terminal-Bench 2.1, 81.2% on FrontierSWE, 42.0% on SWE Marathon, 77.8% on Program Bench). The model ranks #8 of 221 on the Artificial Analysis Intelligence Index with 44, and achieves 93.5% on GPQA Diamond, 81.6% on MMMU-Pro, and 94.3% on MathVision. Kimi K3 is the first open model to reach the 3-trillion-parameter class, with full weights released on July 27, 2026, under a custom Kimi K3 License. The model is priced at $3/$15 per 1M tokens (introductory pricing, with Kimi K3.1 Pro offering $2/$10 per 1M tokens), making it a competitive option for organizations seeking open-weight frontier models with strong performance on coding and agentic tasks.

---

## Model Identity and Background

**Developer:** Moonshot AI (Beijing)
**Release Date:** July 16, 2026 (API), July 27, 2026 (open weights)
**Series:** Kimi K (Kimi K3, Kimi K2.6, Kimi K2.7-Code)
**Predecessor:** Kimi K2.5 (January 2026, retired August 31, 2026)
**Successor:** Kimi K3.1 Pro (October 2026)
**License:** Kimi K3 License (open weights, custom license)
**Context Window:** 1,048,576 tokens
**Max Output:** 64,000 tokens

Kimi K3 is Moonshot AI's flagship mixture-of-experts model from their Kimi series, launched July 16, 2026, with full open weights released on July 27, 2026. The model is designed for complex, long-horizon agentic workflows, featuring a massive 2.8 trillion total parameters (104 billion active per token) and a 1M token context window. Kimi K3 uses Kimi Delta Attention (KDA), Attention Residuals (AttnRes), and Stable LatentMoE architecture, which Moonshot claims improves scaling efficiency by about 2.5 times over Kimi K2. The model was released alongside Kimi K2.6 (cheaper option) and Kimi K2.7-Code (coding specialist). Kimi K3.1 Pro (released October 2026) offers improved performance and lower pricing ($2/$10 per 1M tokens).

