## Availability and Pricing

### Distribution Channels
**Source:** Moonshot AI API documentation
**Snapshot:** 2026

- Available through Moonshot AI API (kimi-k3 model ID)
- Available through Kimi membership plans (Allegro $99, Vivace $199 tiers include full 1M context)
- Available through OpenRouter (21 providers, routing modes: Balanced, Nitro, Floor)
- Available through self-hosting (open weights on Hugging Face, requires 64+ accelerators, 1.56TB checkpoint)

### Pricing Information
**Source:** Moonshot AI API documentation
**Snapshot:** 2026

Standard pricing:
- Input: $3.00 per 1M tokens
- Output: $15.00 per 1M tokens
- Cache read: $0.30 per 1M tokens
- Cache write: 90% discount on input
- Batch API: 50% discount on input and output
- Context window: 1,048,576 tokens (flat pricing, no surcharge)

Pricing comparison:
- Kimi K3: $3/$15 (introductory pricing)
- Kimi K3.1 Pro: $2/$10 (33% cheaper)
- Kimi K2.6: $0.95/$4 (3.5x cheaper)
- Kimi K2.7 Code: $0.95/$4 (3.5x cheaper)
- Kimi K2.5: $0.49 per 1M input (retired August 31, 2026)
- Claude Sonnet 5: $3/$15 (same pricing, but introductory $2/$10 through August 31, 2026)
- Claude Opus 5.5: $4/$20 (1.3x more expensive)
- GPT-6 Astra: $10/$50 (3.3x more expensive)

### Cost Efficiency Analysis
**Source:** Multiple sources
**Snapshot:** 2026

Kimi K3's real cost efficiency depends on:
- Prompt caching usage (90% cost reduction on input tokens)
- Batch API usage (50% discount on input and output)
- Task complexity and length
- Context length (1M tokens)
- Token usage per task (Kimi K3 is more verbose than Kimi K2.6)

The model is positioned as Moonshot AI's flagship model, priced at $3/$15 per 1M tokens. Kimi K3.1 Pro (released October 2026) offers improved performance and lower pricing ($2/$10 per 1M tokens). For cost-sensitive applications, Kimi K2.6 or Kimi K2.7 Code may be more suitable.

